[[31,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/3025600\">5570T90</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025635\">7005A04</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025674\">7005E91</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025665\">7005D24</a></p><p>1. Disconnect the rod from the lock retainer.</p><p>2. Undo the handle retaining bolts.</p><p>3. Release the device (3a) from the retainer (3b) and recover it.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2005133.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[31,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the device is not\ndamaged.</p><p>Secure the device to the retainer.</p><p>Tighten the handle bolts.</p><p>Connect the rod to the lock retainer.</p><p><a href=\"#/3025665\">7005D24</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025674\">7005E91</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025635\">7005A04</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025600\">5570T90</a></p>"]]